					<![CDATA[
						 <div style="text-align: right;"></div> <div class="scp-image-block block-right" style="width:300px;"><img src="http://scp-wiki.wdfiles.com/local--files/scp-5127/SCP-5127.jpg" style="width:300px;" alt="SCP-5127.jpg" class="image" /> <div class="scp-image-caption" style="width:300px;"> <p>SCP-5127</p> </div> </div> <p><strong>Item #:</strong> SCP-5127</p> <p><strong>Object Class:</strong> Keter</p> <p><strong>Special Containment Procedures:</strong> Personnel with appropriate clearance are able to be informed of SCP-5127. Should there be any signs of SCP-5127 approaching planet Earth, O5 Council are to be informed about it immediately.</p> <p><strong>Description:</strong> SCP-5127 is a planet roughly six (6) times bigger than planet Jupiter. SCP-5127's shape is complementary to an oblate spheroid. It appears to look identical to planet Earth. It is believed that one (1) Earth year on SCP-5127 is equal to ten (10) Earth years on Earth. Due to this, SCP-5127's spin speed is roughly 4471&#160;m/s.</p> <p>SCP-5127 does appear to have O<sub>2</sub><sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-36752-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >1</a></sup>. However, SCP-5127 does not appear to be habitable. Should any external object<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-36752-2" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >2</a></sup> be on SCP-5127, the object will dissolve into SCP-5127 and increase its mass. This confirms SCP-5127's sentient properties. SCP-5127 has also been the cause of the destruction of planets such as [DATA EXPUNGED]. Some researchers suggest that SCP-5127 was the cause of the destruction of planet Phaeton<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-36752-3" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >3</a></sup>.</p> <p><strong>Addendum 5127.1:</strong> SCP-5127 has two (2) moons orbiting it: SCP-5127-1 and SCP-5127-2. These moons do not have any abnormalities compared to the moon known as “Luna”. SCP-5127 orbits around a sun that is called SCP-5127-3. SCP-5127-3 has twenty (20) x-class solar flares in one (1) Earth year. Should one occur, it will hit SCP-5127. However, SCP-5127-3's solar flare that hits SCP-5127 makes it larger depending on the size of the flare.</p> <p><strong>Addendum 5127.2:</strong> SCP-5127 was discovered by NASA<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-36752-4" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >4</a></sup> at ██-██-20██. It was discovered that SCP-5127 was moving towards planet Earth.</p> <div class="footnotes-footer"> <div class="title">Footnotes</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-36752-1"><a href="javascript:;" >1</a>. Oxygen.</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-36752-2"><a href="javascript:;" >2</a>. An object that did not originate from SCP-5127, SCP-5127-1, SCP-5127-2 and/or SCP-5127-3.</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-36752-3"><a href="javascript:;" >3</a>. However, Phaeton is a hypothetical planet and Dr. ███████ suggested that Phaeton was destroyed due to centrifugal forces.</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-36752-4"><a href="javascript:;" >4</a>. National Aeronautics and Space Administration</div> </div> <div class="footer-wikiwalk-nav"> <div style="text-align: center;"> <p>&#171; <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5126">SCP-5126</a> | SCP-5127 | <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5128">SCP-5128</a> &#187;</p> </div> </div> <p>by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/gamerboyali" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6944105&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609124846" alt="GamerboyAli" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6944105)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/gamerboyali" >GamerboyAli</a></span></p> 
